# Run in a nested lit by ../../../shlibs.test (M22): %{msil_prog_O2} of a
# program with a cyclic pair of shared libraries (%{msil_shlibs}: b's
# interface, then a, then b) and a file that every run gets (%{msil_deps}).
# The stand-in program calls both libraries when it runs (73 = 1 + 8 + 64),
# so every run needs the build's shlib/ directory beside it.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %t/main.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_shlibs} = ?b=%t/b.c;a=%t/a.c;b=%t/b.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_deps} = %t/dep.txt
# RUN: %{msil_prog_O2}
#--- main.c
// prog-value: 1
#--- a.c
// prog-value: 8
#--- b.c
// prog-value: 64
#--- dep.txt
A file every run gets beside the program.
